<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scyles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Scyles was a Scythian king of the 5th century BCE whose story is told by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>. The son of a Greek mother from Istria, he secretly adopted Greek dress and religion during his visits to the colony of Olbia on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> saw him taking part in Bacchic rites there, they rebelled, and his brother Octamasadas had him beheaded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scyles.jpg" alt="Scyles" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Савелий В А · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2%D0%A1%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BB.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
